# Cursor Rules — Font Intelligence Thin Adapter

This project uses the **Font Intelligence Typography Decision System**.

## Canonical Source of Truth
Consult and follow:
👉 [`.agents/skills/font-intelligence/SKILL.md`](file:///d:/font-intelligence/.agents/skills/font-intelligence/SKILL.md)

## When to Activate
Activate Font Intelligence when:
- Writing or refactoring CSS/SCSS/Tailwind typography rules, `@font-face` definitions, or font variables.
- Designing UI components, web pages, landing pages, dashboards, Flutter apps, or React Native views.
- Selecting, pairing, or styling fonts for any digital or print use case.
- Auditing font readability, licensing, or script coverage.

## Commands & Resources
- CLI Pair Recommender: `python scripts/recommend.py --use-case <id> --style "<vibe>" --platform <web|flutter|powerpoint>`
- Catalog Data: `catalog/fonts.json`, `catalog/use-cases.json`, `catalog/pairings.json`
- Scoring Engine: `scripts/score_pair.py`
- Compact Fallback: [`lite/font-intelligence-lite.md`](file:///d:/font-intelligence/lite/font-intelligence-lite.md)

## Core Guardrails
- Never invent fonts, unverified weights, or unsupported language scripts.
- Never use display/decorative fonts for body or dense UI text.
- Respect explicit user font choices — anchor and pair around them.
- Maximum 2 primary families (heading + body/UI), mono only when required.
- Full protocol: [`.agents/skills/font-intelligence/SKILL.md`](file:///d:/font-intelligence/.agents/skills/font-intelligence/SKILL.md).
